✓ LEXICAL CHANNEL — paired strict delta (answer side, development sample)
  recomputed from the rows' baseline_correct field: +9 gained / −3 regressed (claimed +9/−3)
  29/48 → 35/48 under the both-runs replay rule; exact binomial on 9-vs-3 flips gives p = 0.146.
  Not significant at 0.05. Published at 29/48 → 37/48, p = 0.0215 until the audit of
  2026-09-27/28 overturned two verdicts (see HUMAN AUDIT above).
  ⚠ The vector-only arm (29/48) is ONE run, never replayed. Only the fused arm has two.
  ⚠ This 48-question sample was used during development and runs ~13 points easier than
    its parent set. The transfer evidence is the deterministic holdout below, not this pair.

✓ LEXICAL CHANNEL — the same runs under the FLEXIBLE judge (July's grader)
  34/48 = 70.8% → 37/48 = 77.1%, same both-runs replay rule
  paired: +7 gained / −4 regressed (p = 0.549) — a weaker signal than the strict pair above.
  3 question(s) disagreed between the two runs and were scored by the conjunction.
  Both leniencies are published because a score without its judge is not a result:
  the strict number is the one we lead with, the flexible one is what July would have said.
